{"tool_name":"metab","contents":["bioconda","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"bioconductor-metab","version":"1.33.0","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.17/bioc/html/Metab.html","license":"GPL (>=2)","summary":"Metab: An R Package for a High-Throughput Analysis of Metabolomics Data Generated by GC-MS.","identifiers":["biotools:metab"],"description":"Metab is an R package for high-throughput processing of metabolomics data analysed by the Automated Mass Spectral Deconvolution and Identification System (AMDIS) (http://chemdata.nist.gov/mass-spc/amdis/downloads/). In addition, it performs statistical hypothesis test (t-test) and analysis of variance (ANOVA). Doing so, Metab considerably speed up the data mining process in metabolomics and produces better quality results. Metab was developed using interactive features, allowing users with lack of R knowledge to appreciate its functionalities.","license_file":"/lib/R/share/licenses/GPL-3","build":{"noarch":"generic","number":0,"rpaths":["lib/R/lib/","lib/"]},"requirements":{"host":["bioconductor-xcms >=3.22.0,<3.23.0","r-base","r-pander","r-svdialogs"],"run":["bioconductor-xcms >=3.22.0,<3.23.0","r-base","r-pander","r-svdialogs"]},"source_url":["https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.17/bioc/src/contrib/Metab_1.33.0.tar.gz","https://bioconductor.org/packages/3.17/bioc/src/contrib/Archive/Metab/Metab_1.33.0.tar.gz","https://bioarchive.galaxyproject.org/Metab_1.33.0.tar.gz","https://depot.galaxyproject.org/software/bioconductor-metab/bioconductor-metab_1.33.0_src_all.tar.gz"],"test":{"commands":["$R -e \"library('Metab')\""]},"parent_recipe":{"name":"bioconductor-metab","path":"recipes/bioconductor-metab","version":"1.16.0"}},"biotools":{"id":"metab","home":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/Metab.html","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"R package for high-throughput processing of metabolomics data analysed by the Automated Mass Spectral Deconvolution and Identification System (AMDIS) In addition, it performs statistical hypothesis test (t-test) and analysis of variance (ANOVA). Doing so, it considerably speeds up the data mining process in metabolomics and produces better quality results.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:04:47Z","last_update_date":"2019-06-27T09:03:57Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.8.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:metab","credit":[{"email":"ragg005@aucklanduni.ac.nz","name":"Raphael Aggio","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"http://bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/Metab.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Formatting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0335"},{"term":"Statistical calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2238"}]}],"name":"Metab","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btr379","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: The Automated Mass Spectral Deconvolution and Identification System (AMDIS) is freeware extensively applied in metabolomics. However, datasets processed by AMDIS require extensive data correction, filtering and reshaping to create reliable datasets for further downstream analysis. Performed manually, these processes are laborious and extremely time consuming. Furthermore, manual corrections increase the chance of human error and can introduce additional technical variability to the data. Thus, an automated pipeline for curating GC-MS data is urgently needed.Results: We present the Metab R package designed to automate the pipeline for analysis of metabolomics GC-MS datasets processed by AMDIS. \u00a9 The Author 2011. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Aggio R."},{"name":"Ruggiero K."},{"name":"Villas-Boas S.G."}],"citationCount":86,"date":